Q: only answer nothing to implement: i initially loaded/seeded my portfolio with the wrong tokens and prices. is that an issue? how can i "reset" to my actual buyings from the past 10 years?
A: To rebuild your real 10-year history correctly: once the wrong entries are zeroed out, enter your real historical BUY/SELL transactions one by one, using the purchased_at field for the real date each trade happened (it's separate from recorded_at, which is just "when you typed this in today"). Your current position is just the sum of everything regardless of when it was entered into the system — so backfilling 10 years of real trades today, dated correctly, works exactly as intended. GET /holdings/history lets you verify "what did I actually hold as of date T" afterward.
